I don't want to stop now

15
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,920
It won't be enough

16
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:57,920
I don't want to be able to do it

17
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:01,920
It's the best of the most fun things

18
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:06,920
I don't want to be able to do it

19
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:10,920
I don't want to be able to do it

20
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,920
Say Say Don't

21
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:18,920
今と今向き合って

22
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,920
堪能するよ現実

23
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,920
酸いも甘いも全部

24
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,920
偽不不堂々

25
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,920
正面取ったいらしたいな

26
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,920
面白そうだ

27
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:33,920
喜べそうだよな

28
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,920
今をやめない

29
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:38,920
味わい尽くして笑おう

30
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:48,920
ご視聴ありがとうございました

31
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:49,920
Let's go

32
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:50,920
energía

33
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:56,500
本当に

34
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:15,340
I don't understand how any of that just happened!

35
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,900
Right, that's our cue.

36
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:21,300
Let's go.

37
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:55,740
We messed around too much, Sumo.

38
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:57,940
I think so, Sumo. You're right.

39
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:09,000
Kageyama, did you see my sweet block?

40
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,740
I'm the one who stopped the ball, idiot.

41
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:13,960
Nuh-uh! That was all me, man!

42
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,060
Was not!

43
00:04:15,060 --> 00:04:17,060
Nuh-uh!

44
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:17,260
Nuh-uh!

45
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:18,260
Nuh-uh!

46
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,260
Nuh-uh!

47
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,260
Nuh-uh!

48
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,260
Nuh-uh!

49
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:22,260
Hello?

50
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:23,260
Nuh-uh!

51
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,780
Crap, I got so excited, I forgot what I was gonna say!

52
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:29,980
I'm sorry for calling out of the blue. This is Anabara. And I had to talk to you.

53
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:31,980
I mean, did you?

54
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:32,980
I saw it.

55
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:34,180
It was all right.

56
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:38,180
Oh, right! Yes, of course you did. Can you believe it?

57
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:39,180
Thank you for the game!

58
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:48,180
Karasano High School earns their spot in the top 16. One of this year's favorites in Narazaki High School, led by the Mia Twins, is out after their first match.

59
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:53,380
Only day two of the Spring Nationals, but we've already seen a huge upset in this tournament.

60
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:55,380
Well, guess I'll see you later. Good game.

61
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,380
Uh, yeah.

62
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,380
Hinata!

63
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,380
Huh? What's up?

64
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:07,380
I promise you this. I'm gonna be sent to you one day.

65
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,380
Hm?

66
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:09,380
Hmm.

67
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,380
But before that happens...

68
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:18,580
I am gonna pound your team to dust at the Inner High, so you better be ready.

69
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,580
Rantings of a sore loser.

70
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:26,580
What was that?! I didn't lose! You shut your stupid mouth!

71
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:28,580
What are you doing?!

72
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:30,580
Gather round!

73
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,580
Nice game, you guys!

74
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:34,580
Wow!

75
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,580
That was the best!

76
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:36,580
You were so awesome!

77
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:37,580
Thank you so much!

78
00:05:37,580 --> 00:05:39,580
If we didn't have them cheering for us,

79
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:41,780
Inarizaki would have overpowered us.

80
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:43,780
Thank you so much!

81
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:44,780
Guys!

82
00:05:44,780 --> 00:05:45,780
Thank you for coming!

83
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:49,780
I am so proud to meet you, everyone of you!

84
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:57,780
Let's just get this over with.

85
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,780
We lost and losers don't need applause.

86
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,780
Shut your trap, Hatsulu!

87
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:02,780
Quit!

88
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:03,780
Huh?

89
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,780
That's right!

90
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,780
We see it on your face, but you're wrong!

91
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:07,980
You played good, dumbass!

92
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,980
And every good match deserves praise!

93
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:10,980
Hm!

94
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:11,980
Huh?

95
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:12,980
Huh?

96
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:21,980
Grown-ups like to say it's not about the results.

97
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:22,980
It's about the process.

98
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,980
But you know, kids aren't like that.

99
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,980
I think...

100
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,980
You might be in the minority here, Kida.

101
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:36,180
Thank you for coming!

102
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:43,180
Inarizaki was one of the schools favored to take home the championship.

103
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:45,180
Where do you think things went wrong for your team?

104
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:49,380
I think we may have needed to lean a bit harder on our offense rather than our defense

105
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,180
today, and that was my mistake.

106
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:58,380
But, I have no doubt, my players made great strides in this match.

107
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,380
So, um...

108
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,380
Hm?

109
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,380
We...

110
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,380
We're very sorry.

111
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:14,380
Aren't you trying to make yourselves feel better by apologizing?

112
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:16,380
We're not doing that, okay?

113
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:17,380
Okay, okay.

114
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,380
My mistake.

115
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:23,580
But, if you are, make sure it's when you really feel bad for what you did.

116
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,580
Hm.

117
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:28,580
I have to admit it, I didn't think it was a bad idea to use that quick ride there either.

118
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:30,580
I thought it was gonna get through.

119
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,580
Of course...

120
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:37,580
I do hate it when you try stuff in matches that you haven't actually pulled off in practice.

121
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:38,580
Hm.

122
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:40,580
That last one was just...

123
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:42,580
matched up against the wrong two blockers.

124
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:43,580
I agree.

125
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:45,580
When the two of you really get into it,

126
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:49,780
everyone else on the court usually gets left completely behind.

127
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,780
But this is one of those times where...

128
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:53,780
the guy standing on the other side...

129
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,780
we're really into it too.

130
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:01,780
You were on a high, right?

131
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:02,780
Huh.

132
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:05,780
It's not every day that we get to have a match like that one.

133
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:06,780
Huh.

134
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:07,780
Good for you.

135
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,780
Was Kido just smiling right there?

136
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:12,780
He was.

137
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:15,980
He actually smiled a few times while the match was going on too.

138
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,980
Uh-huh.

139
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,980
No way.

140
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:21,980
But...

141
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:25,980
It does still hurt.

142
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:27,980
Oh...

143
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,980
We did everything that we possibly could.

144
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:33,980
I can honestly say I have no regrets.

145
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,780
I haven't changed my mind either.

146
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:39,180
and I still believe the results are just a by-product.

147
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:41,380
But I don't know.

148
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:45,980
Ugh.

149
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:48,980
I wish...

150
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:51,980
I could've bragged more and said stuff like...

151
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,980
We made it all the way.

152
00:08:53,980 --> 00:09:08,180
We'll make it happen.

153
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:11,180
We'll make sure to become the kind of underclassmen

154
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:13,180
you can brag to your grandkids about.

155
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:17,780
I cannot wait to see that.

156
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,980
Come on.

157
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:20,980
Let's get changed.

158
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:33,980
Tanaka.

159
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:34,980
How long have you been sitting like that?

160
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:35,980
Put your shirt on.

161
00:09:35,980 --> 00:09:36,980
I don't know.

162
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:37,980
Ugh.

163
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:42,180
Suki, you've got two jackets on!

164
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,180
Huh?

165
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:47,180
I think this might be the first time I've seen Tsukishima about to shut down.

166
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,180
Did a lot of work out there today.

167
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,180
Makes sense.

168
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,180
Huh?

169
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:51,180
Huh?

170
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,180
Nishinoya!

171
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,180
Don't fall asleep there!

172
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,180
And yet now,

173
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:59,180
the one who usually passes out first is still wide awake.

174
00:09:59,180 --> 00:09:59,780
Yeah.

175
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,180
Hmm?

176
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:04,180
Maybe all the moving around actually made it so he can't sleep.

177
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:10,380
Today, I'm pretty sure I witnessed someone having that moment.

178
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:21,380
Day two of spring nationals.

179
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:28,380
The day this shrimp got even more hooked and fell deeper in love with volleyball.

180
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:42,020
Afternoon

181
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:51,580
Yeah!

182
00:10:51,580 --> 00:10:52,580
Hey!

183
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,580
Kuratsuno beat the Miyas.

184
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,580
Come on, man.

185
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:56,580
You really didn't know?

186
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:58,080
Didn't you hear all the screaming?

187
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:01,700
I don't pay attention to what's going on outside of my match.

188
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,960
Anyway, Karasuno won and one of the favorites is going home now.

189
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:09,280
Oh, that sucks. I really wanted to play against those freaks.

190
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,720
Today, Bokuto was definitely concentrating.

191
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:19,660
He wasn't all there during our first set yesterday, but he's been in great form ever since.

192
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,880
No, I need to stop it.

193
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:27,620
If I keep thinking about this and start getting greedy, I have a feeling something will go wrong.

194
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,320
Detached. I need to remain detached.

195
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,880
Akashi's overthinking things again.

196
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:40,540
That was amazing! I think I might be turning into a Karasuno fan now.

197
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:43,540
So what team will they be going up against in their next match?

198
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:45,540
Nekumahai.

199
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:49,280
Hey, that's the same team that you guys had to play, isn't it?

200
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,860
Which of them do you think will win?

201
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:57,320
I'm not really sure, but I don't think anyone should underestimate Karasuno's momentum.

202
00:11:57,740 --> 00:12:00,380
Oh, that makes sense.

203
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,140
I mean, Karasuno is on a roll, after all.

204
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:05,920
What do you want to do tomorrow? Should we come watch?

205
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,340
Yeah, okay, why not?

206
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:09,040
Did you have fun today, Mika?

207
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,400
Oh, yes. I can't wait for Karasuno's match tomorrow.

208
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,880
It can't be easy stopping that attack.

209
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:20,880
I know, right? And this Nekumah team they're up against seems sort of bland by comparison.

210
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:22,340
They're totally no match for Karasuno.

211
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,340
It'll be a piece of cake.

212
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:27,340
Oh, you are going to eat those words, lady!

213
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:36,340
And that concludes our story about the cat and the jealous snake.

214
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:39,020
Ha, ha, ha. It must be hard being that snake.

215
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:42,640
Ha, now moving on to sports. Over to you, Yamashita.

216
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,240
Here it is.

217
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:47,280
I'm here at round two of the Haruko National High School Volleyball Championship.

218
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:50,680
The seeded teams begin play for both the girls and the boys' brackets.

219
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,080
On the boys' side, we saw a major upset.

220
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,380
Ha, ha, ha.

221
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:59,980
Game two on port A was between an Arasaki High School led by the unstoppable Mia Twins

222
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:04,220
and an old contender from the Tohoku region, Karasuno High School,

223
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,640
a team with a heavy emphasis on offense.

224
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:11,480
They have their own all-Japan youth-intensive invitee, Tobio Kageyama.

225
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:15,760
Ah, the Mia Twins gave Karasuno some trouble with their flawless teamwork.

226
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,360
While the leader of Karasuno's charge was Ryunosuke Tanaka,

227
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,940
who may have been trying a bit too hard as he couldn't get his game done.

228
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:25,080
Ha, ha, ha. That hurts me.

229
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:29,700
Then, in the second set, Karasuno's blocker struggled to stop the quick attacks

230
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:32,340
of an Arasaki middle blocker, Rintaro Sula.

231
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:34,240
On purpose? We were doing it on purpose!

232
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:35,780
Tadashi, shut up.

233
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:40,220
Karasuno could not take the second set, but they showed remarkable tenacity in the fire.

234
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:40,820
Oh, that's me! I'm on TV!

235
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,980
Holy crap, your face, Suga!

236
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,280
Yeah, that's not a great look.

237
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:47,900
Hey, Kyoko!

238
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:52,960
Hey, they're totally giving Kyoko more screen time.

239
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,200
Oh, beautiful!

240
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,480
Hey, Sasaki!

241
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,420
You look like you've killed a man or two in that shot.

242
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,720
Man, you look rad!

243
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,120
Is that how I look when I concentrate?

244
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,100
You should see him in math class.

245
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:15,840
Look! There it is! See that? My awesome receive!

246
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,260
You see that, Kageyama?

247
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:17,720
Missed it.

248
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,740
Then look, butthead!

249
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:19,800
There's his or she!

250
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:20,500
Shut up!

251
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:21,640
So embarrassing!

252
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:31,220
This isn't like you, Bokuto.

253
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:33,520
Are you not gonna watch the news?

254
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:33,940
Hmm?

255
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,440
I did, remember?

256
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:38,200
I mean, I thought you'd watch it a hundred times on repeat.

257
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,980
Hey, what kind of person do you think I am exactly?

258
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:44,900
I wasn't on camera all that much tonight. Twenty times is more than enough.

259
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:47,600
Oh, so he's showing some restraint.

260
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:58,920
But, well, I'm still gonna be playing volleyball after high school, so I didn't think this being my last high school tournament would make it that much different from any of the others.

261
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:06,460
But man, I really wish I could play a lot more with you guys.

262
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:08,360
Huh?

263
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:11,180
You're not dying, are you, Bokuto?

264
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:12,120
What?

265
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:12,900
No!

266
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:14,780
I'm gonna live to be 130.

267
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:17,820
Then what are you talking about?

268
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,480
This is only day two of the tournament.

269
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:23,600
Third round, quarterfinals, then semifinals, and then finals.

270
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,460
We still have a lot of games ahead of us.

271
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:27,840
Yeah?

272
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:31,720
And we're gonna win them all.

273
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:37,640
Hmm.

274
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:40,480
All right, we better get inside.

275
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,960
It's flu and norovirus season.

276
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:45,140
You can't underestimate January.

277
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:46,560
What?

278
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:47,960
It's January?

279
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:49,520
Man.

280
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:52,120
Kageyama just gets more and more amazing.

281
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:54,800
I think I'm just gonna ask him for his autograph now.

282
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:57,620
No way that guy's come up with an autograph yet.

283
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,580
Not sure he can spell it.

284
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:01,900
Okay, I'll come up with one for him.

285
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,760
We can even finish it with a heart.

286
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,460
That's perfect, he'll love it.

287
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:07,440
And Tanaka played great today, too.

288
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:09,020
That cut shot?

289
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,540
Followed by that razor-sharp line shot.

290
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:17,940
And that rebound toward the end was insane.

291
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:21,480
He seems like the last person who could ever play so in control.

292
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:24,480
Speaking of control, what about Tsukishima?

293
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:28,420
The way he narrows down the attacker's options without even breaking a sweat?

294
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,280
What is he, some kind of artiste?

295
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,100
Yeah, I definitely would have tried to hit the ball there.

296
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,940
Oh, and man, then Hinata's received.

297
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:37,460
A total shocker.

298
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:39,120
That dig was something else.

299
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:44,020
But on that last point we played, when Hinata bumped Tanaka's rebound up in the air...

300
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:44,360
Yeah!

301
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,400
That was him, wasn't it?

302
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:47,560
It was awesome.

303
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,720
I totally cried.

304
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:52,320
Well, I can't blame you, but you know what?

305
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:57,680
Watching those guys grow over this last year, can't let them steal the show.

306
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:02,060
Oh, yeah, and of course, you never want to let the other team win.

307
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,900
But we don't want to beat ourselves, either.

308
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:04,620
Exactly.

309
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:07,940
Don't go trying to show them up with a wicked cross shot tomorrow.

310
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,160
What are you talking about?

311
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,300
You know I don't have the balls for that.

312
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,600
Well, you gotta get some.

313
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,200
Or at least lie and say you do.

314
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:17,360
Sounds like you know a lot about balls.

315
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:18,600
I am, I'm a baller.

316
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:19,560
You think so, huh?

317
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,120
Ooh, I know that soap.

318
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,600
It smells really good.

319
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:25,720
Oh, yeah?

320
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:27,960
All the girls in my class use it.

321
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:33,320
It's really nice, but I heard you're actually not supposed to wash your face and body with it too hard.

322
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:35,020
What?

323
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:37,120
But I always rub as hard as possible!

324
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:41,440
Well, I'll try to wash myself just like you do tomorrow.

325
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:41,820
Huh?

326
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:47,340
It'd be embarrassing if you watched me that closely.

327
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,940
You're sure full of energy today, Hinata.

328
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,900
I'm still excited for our match!

329
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,680
I want to play the next one right now!

330
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:09,560
You are a lunatic.

331
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,340
Come on, Tsukishima!

332
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,520
That wasn't sarcasm!

333
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:13,240
You meant it!

334
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,020
Now you're hurting my feelings!

335
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:20,340
What was that for?

336
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,040
You're obnoxious.

337
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:21,460
Hinata!

338
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:23,880
Your face is obnoxious!

339
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:33,860
Stalwart has always been a good word to describe Nekoma High School, but with a new high-powered middle blocker in their ranks, they're bringing both their offense and defense to new heights.

340
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:38,700
And with Karasuno building momentum, I really hope they'll at least be able to put up a good place...

341
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:42,160
Listen, jackass! Don't you try and make it sound like we're the weak ones!

342
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:45,360
Well, everyone does think that Karasuno is better than us.

343
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:45,880
What?!

344
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:47,800
Since they've beaten so many tough schools.

345
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:50,020
Screw that! We've defeated tough schools, too!

346
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,780
That's the whole reason we even got here!

347
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:54,260
I also see you only got a futon out for yourself!

348
00:18:54,260 --> 00:19:00,320
Well, think about this. You really believe we could have beaten Ushiwaka or the Mia Twins like them?

349
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:05,200
Hey, don't just leave it at that!

350
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:08,040
I think we'll never know until we try, dude!

351
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:12,340
And while Rock may always crush scissors, it'll never be able to beat Paper!

352
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:15,620
Well, it doesn't matter what anyone thinks.

353
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:16,160
Hmm?

354
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:21,160
Because we came here specifically to play those guys and find out who's better.

355
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:27,120
As far as Kenma goes, I really don't think he'll be too bothered if they lose.

356
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:28,020
Huh?

357
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:32,000
But me? I want to win!

358
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:38,980
Wow, it's already dark?

359
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:42,760
So sorry I'm late, Akane. I got caught up in a conversation earlier.

360
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:44,840
It's okay. I just called my mom.

361
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:45,720
Uh-huh.

362
00:19:51,160 --> 00:20:21,140
Oh, come on, come on, come on, come on!

363
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:51,140
Oh, come on, come on!

364
00:20:51,160 --> 00:21:21,140
Oh, come on, come on, come on!

365
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:51,140
Oh, come on, come on!

366
00:21:51,160 --> 00:22:21,140
Oh, oh, oh.

367
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:35,220
I guess I finally got to have my own classic game.

368
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,740
So your own dumpster showdown, eh?

369
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:41,980
Hmm?

370
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:47,280
You know, for a long, long time, I really thought I knew how to teach anybody anything.

371
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,980
I thought that it'd be easy.

372
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:53,700
You see, son, I wanted my boys to do what I would have done, or what I wished I could

373
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:53,980
do.

374
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:59,100
And one day, I started wondering how they thought about things.

375
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,360
They're not me.

376
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,500
They're not my pawns.

377
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:09,300
Once I finally realized that obvious fact, I stopped pretending that I could teach people

378
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,200
and started actually teaching them.

379
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:14,500
And boy, did that ever turn out to be a tough path for me to take.

380
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:21,120
But you, you're a natural at teaching.

381
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:21,880
What?

382
00:23:22,260 --> 00:23:24,180
Good thing you suck at the playing part.

383
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:25,320
Uh, what?

384
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:32,000
You think I want to do this dumpster showdown out of some sense of duty to my family?

385
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:37,440
Right now, the ones who want to beat Nekoma more than anyone else are my boys.

386
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:41,900
And let me tell you, Nekoma is not the team we had that old feud with anymore.

387
00:23:42,420 --> 00:23:46,220
So please just try thinking of it as something fun this time, okay?

388
00:23:46,220 --> 00:24:16,200
Nekoma is not the team we had that old feud with anymore.

